<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Turin</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Torino, Augusta Taurinorum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Turin is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> on the Po river and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>. Founded as the Roman colony of Augusta Taurinorum, it became the capital of the dukes of Savoy in 1563 and later of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>. It led the unification of Italy and was the first capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> from 1861 to 1865, before growing into a major industrial city as the home of FIAT.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/turin.jpg" alt="Turin" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zairon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Torino_Piazza_Castello_11.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
